    {
      "id": "jshell-501-method-refs",
      "type": "CODE",
      "mode": "jshell",
      "source": "//@ anchor: the-4-kinds-of-method-references\n//@ description: The 4 kinds of method references\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.function.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\n// --- The 4 kinds of method references ---\n// When a lambda does nothing but call one existing method, a method reference says\n// the same thing with less noise. There are exactly four forms.\n\n// 1. STATIC method: ClassName::staticMethod\n//    same as: s -> Integer.parseInt(s)\nFunction<String, Integer> parse = Integer::parseInt;\nSystem.out.println(\"parseInt('42') = \" + parse.apply(\"42\"));\n\n// 2. Method on a SPECIFIC instance: instance::method\n//    same as: s -> prefix.concat(s). `prefix` is captured, so it is fixed for the\n//    life of the function - the receiver is decided here, not at call time.\nString prefix = \"BARISTA-\";\nFunction<String, String> addPrefix = prefix::concat;\nSystem.out.println(\"addPrefix('007') = \" + addPrefix.apply(\"007\"));\n\n// 3. Method on an ARBITRARY instance of a type: ClassName::instanceMethod\n//    same as: s -> s.toUpperCase(). This looks identical to form 1 but means\n//    something different: the function's ARGUMENT becomes the receiver.\nFunction<String, String> upper = String::toUpperCase;\nFunction<String, String> trim  = String::trim;\nSystem.out.println(\"upper('hello')   = \" + upper.apply(\"hello\"));\n\n// 4. CONSTRUCTOR: ClassName::new\n//    same as: s -> new StringBuilder(s). Which constructor is chosen depends on the\n//    functional interface's shape - here, the one taking a single String.\nFunction<String, StringBuilder> newSB = StringBuilder::new;\nStringBuilder sb = newSB.apply(\"initial\");\nSystem.out.println(\"StringBuilder = \" + sb);\n\n// Form 3 is the one that shows up constantly in streams: each element in turn\n// becomes the receiver of the method.\nList<String> raw = List.of(\"  alice  \", \"  BOB  \", \" charlie \");\nList<String> cleaned = raw.stream()\n    .map(String::trim)            // (3) each element is the receiver\n    .map(String::toLowerCase)     // (3) again\n    .collect(Collectors.toList());\nSystem.out.println(\"cleaned = \" + cleaned);",
      "output": "",
      "returnValue": null,
      "executed": false,
      "executionCount": null,
      "error": "",
      "anchor": "the-4-kinds-of-method-references",
